questions.stem:
A mountain lodge dims its lamps with this fragment:
abstract class Lantern { abstract String glow(); String show() { return "soft-" + glow(); } }
class Beacon extends Lantern { String glow() { return "beam"; } }
Lantern l = new Beacon();
System.out.print(l.show());
What is printed?

A brickyard fires its kilns with this fragment:
class Kiln { Kiln() { System.out.print("fire-"); } }
class BrickKiln extends Kiln { BrickKiln() { System.out.print("brick"); } }
new BrickKiln();
What is printed?

An orchard app tracks harvests with this subclass, where Fruit(String orchard) stores the grove name:
public class OrchardApple extends Fruit {
  private int crates;
  OrchardApple(String orchard, int crates) { _____; this.crates = crates; }
}
Which line belongs in the blank?

A greenhouse roster fails to compile here:
class Sprout extends Seed {
  Sprout() { System.out.print("warm"); super(); }
}
What is the fault?

A seed library stacks three growers with this fragment:
class Plot { Plot() { System.out.print(1); } }
class Row extends Plot { Row() { System.out.print(2); } }
class Bed extends Row { Bed() { System.out.print(3); } }
new Bed();
The digits print with no spaces or newline. What integer is printed?

A parade marshal measures horns with this fragment:
class Horn { int decibels() { return 40; } }
class Trumpet extends Horn { int decibels() { return 90; } }
static int loudness(Horn h) { return h.decibels(); }
System.out.print(loudness(new Trumpet()) + loudness(new Horn()));
What integer is printed?

A rescue shelter places either a turtle or a parrot with this helper:
_____ place(boolean calm) { return calm ? new Turtle() : new Parrot(); }
Both Turtle and Parrot extend Pet. Which signature belongs in the blank?

A cliff aviary fails to compile here:
class Aviary { Bird fetch() { return new Bird(); } }
class Cage extends Aviary { String fetch() { return "wren"; } }
What is the fault?

A bell foundry totals tones with this fragment:
interface Chime { int tone(); }
class Bell implements Chime { public int tone() { return 5; } }
class Gong implements Chime { public int tone() { return 9; } }
Chime[] rack = {new Bell(), new Gong(), new Bell()};
int t = 0;
for (Chime c : rack) t += c.tone();
System.out.println(t);
What integer is printed?

A harbor crew tests towing with this fragment:
class Engine { int thrust() { return 8; } }
class Tug { Engine e = new Engine(); int pull() { return e.thrust() + 2; } }
System.out.print(new Tug().pull());
What integer is printed?

A hiking club notes each backpack has a sleeping bag, and a backpack is not a kind of sleeping bag:
class Backpack {
  _____;
}
Which line belongs in the blank?

A meadow field guide is reviewed here:
class Sparrow extends Wings { }
A sparrow is not a kind of wings; it has wings. What is the fault?

A freight dock sorts crates with this fragment:
class Crate implements Comparable<Crate> {
  int kg;
  Crate(int kg) { this.kg = kg; }
  public int compareTo(Crate o) { return Integer.compare(this.kg, o.kg); }
}
Crate[] dock = {new Crate(12), new Crate(7), new Crate(20)};
Arrays.sort(dock);
The weights print in order separated by spaces. What is printed?

A seed vault orders packets by sprouting days:
class SeedPacket implements Comparable<SeedPacket> {
  int days;
  public int compareTo(SeedPacket o) { _____; }
}
Which body belongs in the blank?

A parcel hub mis-sorts extreme codes with this method:
public int compareTo(Parcel o) { return this.code - o.code; }
Codes near the integer limits order backwards. What is the fault?

A sprout lab scores three packets with days p1 = 9, p2 = 4, p3 = 14, using Integer.compare on days:
int s = Integer.compare(p1, p2) + Integer.compare(p2, p3) + Integer.compare(p1, p3);
System.out.println(s);
What integer is printed?
